# Branch naming

All branches must follow the pattern:

```
KAN-{ticket-number}-{short-description}
```

## Rules

1. Always prefix with the Jira ticket key (`KAN-{number}`)
2. Short description: lowercase, hyphen-separated, 2-4 words
3. No spaces, no uppercase, no special characters

## Examples

- `KAN-18-project-rules`
- `KAN-19-scryfall-ingest`
- `KAN-20-resolver-cascade`

## When creating a branch

Follow the full **new task workflow** in `new-task-workflow.mdc` (verify trunk → Jira ticket → branch).

Branch pattern only:

```bash
git checkout -b KAN-{n}-{description}
```

Always create the branch from an up-to-date `1-production`.

## Note on the shared board

The `KAN` project is shared with prizeWallAnalyzer, so ticket numbers are sequential across both. That keeps every key globally unique — `KAN-19` means one thing only. Tickets for this project carry the `collection-manager` label.
